+              your domain. When a message arrives, the receiving server reads your SPF record and checks the
+              sender against it. Together with DKIM and DMARC, SPF stops spammers from forging your domain and
+              keeps your legitimate mail out of the spam folder. Use the checker above to see your record exactly
+              as receiving servers do.
+            </p>
+          </section>
+          <section>
+            <h2 className="text-2xl font-black text-foreground mb-3">How to check an SPF record</h2>
