+              <li>Fix any warnings, wait for DNS to propagate, and check again.</li>
+            </ol>
+          </section>
+          <section>
+            <h2 className="text-2xl font-black text-foreground mb-3">SPF, DKIM and DMARC work together</h2>
+            <p>
+              SPF verifies the sending server, DKIM signs the message content, and DMARC tells receivers what to
+              do when the first two fail — and gives you reports. Passing SPF alone is a start; a DMARC policy of{" "}
+              <span className="font-mono">p=reject</span> with aligned SPF and DKIM is the end state that makes
+              spoofing your domain impractical. Check where your mail actually enters with the{" "}
+              <Link to="/mx-lookup" className="text-emerald-600 font-semibold hover:underline">MX Lookup</Link> and
+              the full stack with{" "}
+              <Link to="/email" className="text-emerald-600 font-semibold hover:underline">Email Diagnostics</Link>.
